cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its frozen evidence chain, please cite it using
  the metadata below.
title: "AirSense V2 — causal multi-horizon PM2.5 forecasting under a sealed final test"
abstract: >-
  A leakage-controlled multi-horizon PM2.5 forecasting study over twelve Beijing
  monitoring stations, evaluated once on a chronologically sealed final test
  block under a confirmatory hierarchy frozen before the test was opened. The
  repository carries the full evidence chain: per-phase freezes, manifests,
  hash-pinned model artifacts and prediction arrays, twelve validators and an
  independent recomputation path. Engineered causal history improved on causal
  persistence on average across 1-24 hours; persistence remained the strongest
  severe-tail benchmark.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chakraborty
    given-names: Debalekha
repository-code: "https://github.com/DebalekhaChakraborty/AirSense"
url: "https://github.com/DebalekhaChakraborty/AirSense"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - PM2.5 forecasting
  - air quality
  - multi-horizon time-series forecasting
  - causal forecasting
  - chronological generalisation
  - severe pollution episodes
  - reproducible machine learning
  - evaluation governance
